 "tree_share": 0.6,
 "_about_tree": "(polish1 D4d) Up in the treetop village and on the offshore complex: while the prey an enemy is sent for stands on a deck (layer 1 / 2 / 3; the offshore complex counts as 3), `tree_share` of the round's enemies (and every crab: crabs cannot climb) are drawn from that layer's `tree_mix` instead (from round `from`). `climbs` = it climbs trunks and stilts to the decks (core/treetop_rules.gd climbs, at `climb_speed` m/s); `flies` = a glider that comes out of the sky (`comes` sky) and cruises `cruise` m over its prey between swoops; `cuts` = it goes for a bought rope bridge or rope ladder and cuts it in `cut_seconds` (players mend it by holding interact, free). The *_tough enemies are the old ones grown bigger and stronger (`tough_of`) that climb."
}